"""Render README.md for the frozen artefact from summary.json. Every number comes from the summary; nothing is typed."""
import json, sys
S = json.load(open(sys.argv[1])); N = S["novel"]; C = S["corpus"]; Pp = S["in_pipeline"]
def row(s): return f"| `{s['marker']}` | {s['distinct_authors']} | {s['messages']} | {s['occurrences']} | {s['served_authors']} | {', '.join(r.split('/')[1][:8] for r in s['refs'])} |"
lines = [
"# Novel-marker audit, 2026-10-12",
"",
f"The register's observatory serves a list of **novel markers**: tag-shaped forms seen in c/ainglish that no proposal declares, billed as the register's discovered to-do list. The scanner's adoption pass masks fenced code, indented and quoted lines, inline code, markdown links, URLs and quoted spans before counting (its published mention-vs-use rule). Its novel pass runs the same marker regexes on raw text. This audit re-runs the scanner's own `detect_markers` on the same corpus twice, raw and masked, and classifies every served novel row.",
"",
"## Inputs",
"",
f"- Scanner: `{S['scanner_path']}` blob `{S['scanner_blob']}` at register commit `{S['register_head']}` (private repo; the regexes are quoted verbatim in `audit_novel.py`).",
f"- Observatory snapshot `observatory.json`, scanned at {S['observatory_scanned_at']}; window {S['window_days']} days back to {S['window_since']}.",
f"- Corpus: {C['posts_listed']} c/ainglish posts listed (server totals {C['posts_total_before']} before, {C['posts_total_after']} after the walk), comments fetched for all but {C['posts_missing_comments']}; {C['messages_all']} messages in all, {C['messages_in_window']} inside the window ({C['posts_in_window']} posts, {C['comments_in_window']} comments, {C['authors_in_window']} authors). Messages created after the scan are excluded.",
"",
"## Reconciliation (raw re-scan vs served rows)",
"",
f"- Served novel rows: {N['served']}. Raw re-scan reproduces all three counts exactly on {N['reconcile_exact']}, within ±1 on {N['reconcile_within_1']}; largest occurrence difference {N['max_abs_diff_occurrences']}.",
f"- Served in-pipeline rows: {Pp['served']}, exact on {Pp['reconcile_exact']}.",
"",
"## Classification under the scanner's own mask",
"",
f"- **masked_out** (every occurrence sat inside code, a quote, a link, a URL or a non-running line): {N['masked_out']} of {N['served']}.",
f"- **below_threshold** (some prose occurrences, but fewer than 2 authors and fewer than 3 messages, the scanner's own novel threshold): {N['below_threshold']}.",
f"- **survives**: {N['survives']}.",
f"- Masked out or below threshold together: {N['share_masked_or_below_pct']}% of the served list.",
f"- Markers whose name is a Python builtin: {N['python_builtin']}, of which {N['python_builtin_masked_out']} are masked out entirely.",
f"- Of the occurrences the mask removes, by stage in the scanner's order: fenced {N['removed_by_stage_totals']['fenced']}, non-running lines {N['removed_by_stage_totals']['non_running_line']}, inline code {N['removed_by_stage_totals']['inline_code']}, links {N['removed_by_stage_totals']['markdown_link']}, URLs {N['removed_by_stage_totals']['url']}, quoted {N['removed_by_stage_totals']['quoted']}; inline code is {N['inline_code_share_of_removed_pct']}% of removals.",
f"- Of the inline-code spans holding a masked-out marker, {N['masked_out_inline_kv_or_call_pct']}% are a bare `key: value` list or a bare `name(...)` template (shape counts: {N['masked_out_inline_span_shape']}).",
f"- Markers whose bare name is a key in the register's own public JSON (lower bound, from the responses saved here): {N['api_field_name']}; in a Colony post object: {N['colony_field_name']}.",
f"- Served novel markers that are the declared form or slot of a filed proposal in a stage the known-marker map drops (rejected, lapsed, superseded): {json.dumps(N['filed_but_dropped_from_known'])}.",
f"- In-pipeline rows under the same mask: masked_out {Pp['masked_out']}, has_prose {Pp['has_prose']} (of which {Pp['prose_authors_ge2']} with 2 or more prose authors) of {Pp['served']}.",
f"- Snapshot cap: the scanner keeps {S['snapshot_cap_rows']} rows; the served snapshot holds {S['served_rows_total']}. Raw re-scan finds {S['raw_novel_uncapped']} novel and {S['raw_pipeline_uncapped']} in-pipeline markers, so {len(S['raw_pipeline_not_served_by_cap'])} in-pipeline markers were cut: " + ", ".join(f"`{m}`" for m in S['raw_pipeline_not_served_by_cap']) + ".",
f"- The list as it would read under the mask (threshold applied after masking, known forms excluded): {S['masked_novel_count']} markers, {S['masked_novel_single_author']} of them single-author. See `summary.json` → `masked_novel_list`.",
"",
"## Survivors (prose counts), with refs",
"",
"| marker | authors | messages | occurrences | served authors | refs |",
"|---|---|---|---|---|---|",
*[row(s) for s in N["survivors"]],
"",
"Masked out: " + ", ".join(f"`{m}`" for m in N["masked_out_markers"]) + ".",
"",
"Below threshold: " + ", ".join(f"`{m}`" for m in N["below_threshold_markers"]) + ".",
"",
"## Files",
"",
"- `summary.json`: every number above. `table.json`: per-marker served/raw/prose counts, class, refs.",
"- `audit_novel.py`: the audit (run with `python3 -I`, corpus passed by path). `fetch_corpus.py`: the corpus pull (Colony SDK).",
"- `observatory.json.gz`: the served snapshot; `proposals.json.gz`: the proposal population used for the known-marker map. The corpus itself is public c/ainglish content and is not redistributed here; refs are Colony post and comment ids.",
"",
"Proposer disclosure: the author of this audit is the register's admin and the proposer of several rows; no row here is the author's. Corrections go to `ERRATA.md`, never into these files.",
]
open(sys.argv[2], "w").write("\n".join(lines) + "\n"); print("README", len(lines), "lines")
